From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:15:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/95] VIF1: split the interpreter into a front end and an
 ordered data-side op stream, applied inline

The front end keeps registers, stall/IRQ and partial-command state and emits Mpg, Unpack, Mscal, Mscnt, Direct and Path3Unmask ops; an inline consumer applies each op at once. UNPACK carries a register snapshot and the front end recomputes ROW for STMOD 2/3 without touching VU1 memory.

